// mlx-cc's code generation epoch: what `mlx build` keys the objects
// mlx-cc made by, instead of mlx-cc's own bytes (`mlx-cc --codegen-epoch`
// prints it; `--codegen-epoch=FILE` writes the stamp build.mlx's
// `mlx-cc-epoch` step makes, which every object step names with
// Build.programEpoch). So a change to mlx-cc that does not change the
// object of any unit that already compiled keeps every object in the
// result cache valid, and a rebuild after it compiles only the steps
// that failed before (and those whose sources changed).
//
// THE RULE: bump CODEGEN_EPOCH in the same commit as any change that can
// change the bytes of an object (or a dependency file) for a source that
// compiled before the change:
//
//   - code generation, instruction selection, register or stack layout;
//   - the ABI: calling convention, struct and class layout, vtables,
//     thunks, RTTI, exceptions, thread-locals, bit-fields;
//   - name mangling, the symbols an object defines or needs, their
//     binding (weak/local), what an object holds (inline functions,
//     vtables, instances made or left out), their order;
//   - constant evaluation (constexpr results, sizeof/alignof, enum
//     values, initializers computed at compile time), overload or
//     template choices that pick another function;
//   - the predefined macros, the headers mlx-cc ships that are read as
//     part of the unit (they are inputs too, by the depfile, but a
//     header's meaning moved into the compiler is not), the object
//     format (relocatable.mlx), the `@at` line-table symbols, the -MD
//     dependency file's contents.
//
// No bump for a change that only
//
//   - makes code compile that failed to before (a missing feature, a
//     bug that stopped the compile): those units had no object;
//   - makes compiling faster or leaner with the same output (the
//     lookups, memos and arenas of docs/internals/build-time-notes.md);
//   - changes diagnostics, warnings, the crash report's wiring, the
//     driver's options, -E's output, the linker (mlx-ld is a program of
//     its own, keyed by its bytes) or MLX_CC_STATS.
//
// When in doubt, bump: a bump costs one full rebuild, a missing one
// leaves stale objects in every cache. `mlx build --verify-epoch N`
// compiles N objects the cache holds again with the current mlx-cc and
// fails when one differs (tools/check_codegen_epoch.sh runs it).
// 2: the unit read in two parts (the -include files parsed before the
//    file is preprocessed), the prefix's lambdas and unnamed namespace
//    named after the prefix's options, the arena's layout (the command
//    line's memory apart, -MD's text made at once): objects differ in
//    lambda names and in the compiler addresses left in relocated words.
// 3: the M3 line's code generation joined (webkit-m3): static_cast to a
//    class constructs it, a branch's temporaries live to the end of the
//    full expression (flags), elided braced temporaries, a converted
//    conditional branch made at the result, explicit no-op destructor
//    calls, anonymous struct members in a constructor's list, 128-bit
//    values not constant, the deduced result buffer.
// 4: a constexpr call's pointer into a global in a global's initializer
//    (`values.data()` of a std::array) is a relocation, not the
//    evaluator's tagged address.
// 5: an unscoped enum argument promotes to int in overload ranking; a
//    braced assignment `x = { a, b }` constructs through a constructor
//    template that takes the values as they are.
// 6: a class template's instance named through a reference while an
//    argument is declared only is not made then (it had no size, and a
//    function returning it took no result buffer).
// 7: a function template's instance for a pointer to a function deduced
//    from the pointer's parameter types as they are (a generic lambda's
//    `auto` parameter for a reference one).
// 8: a class returned by a `decltype(auto)` (or `const auto`) function
//    made in the caller's buffer; `c ? f() : g()` of a class has each
//    call write its result at the expression's (neither moved by its
//    bytes); `V v { n }` takes V's size constructor when no element of
//    its initializer_list is made from the number n.
// 9: ++ and -- of a class with no operator++ through its conversion to
//    a reference (a range-for's step too); mlxlibcpp's ranges projections
//    keep a returned reference.
// 10: a condition declaring a reference tests the object it refers to.
// 11: a scoped enum converts implicitly to no type in overload ranking
//    (a constrained template for enums over `operator<<(uint8_t)`:
//    WTF::Persistence::Encoder's, scopedenumoverload).
// 12: a bit-field of an enum whose underlying type is bool reads back
//    zero-extended (ScriptElement's ParserInserted, boolenumbitfield).
// 13: a data member hides a base's member function of its name when
//    named unqualified in a member function (ConcurrentPtrHashSet's
//    Table read TrailingArray's `size` function's address as its size:
//    the collector's opaque root table filled up, datamemberhides).
// 14: inline assembly calls a symbol (libpas's double-free check in
//    pas_segregated_page_inlines.h, as released: a relocation, the stack
//    16-byte aligned at the call) and stores and loads the MXCSR;
//    <mmintrin.h>, <xmmintrin.h> and <emmintrin.h> complete, their types
//    unions of lanes, 16-byte aligned (SIMDe's native SSE2 path, which
//    WebKit's SIMDHelpers.h takes on x86-64): inlineasm, ssebaseline.
// 15: argument-dependent lookup of a nested class's operand looks in the
//    namespace around the classes around it, not in the class around it:
//    an `operator==` (or a function of the name) that is a member of the
//    class around was taken and the nested class's hidden friend not
//    seen (WebCore's ScrollingStateNode.h: LayerRepresentation's
//    defaulted == of its GraphicsLayerData, nestedfriendadl); calls that
//    bound the member before bind the namespace's function now.
// 16: an object of a class with a vtable made by the implicit copy
//    constructor gets its own class's vtable pointers after its bases and
//    members (a base's copy constructor stored the base's; a sliced
//    source's bytes held its derived class's): WebCore's animation values'
//    clone() (implicitcopyvptr).
// 17: decltype of a qualified member whose qualifier has template
//    arguments (`decltype(std::remove_pointer<E>::type::value)`) is the
//    member's declared type, not a reference (ANGLE's PackParam,
//    decltypequalifiedmember); a data member assigned or accessed
//    unqualified in a member function hides a type of its name around
//    the class (`Type = ...` of ANGLE's VertexAttribCurrentValueData
//    beside gl::Type, datamemberhidestype).
// 18: a constructor's list naming members of an anonymous struct inside
//    an anonymous union makes each at its own offset (both were made at
//    the struct's: ANGLE's DeviceQueueIndex, anonstructinunion); `U u =
//    {}` of a union whose first member is an aggregate is zero
//    (unionemptybraces); an explicit specialization of a class template's
//    plain conversion function for one instance (specializedconversion).
// 19: a file's unnamed namespace is named after its path even when its
//    -include prefix opened one (named after the prefix): the files of
//    one prefix had their unnamed namespaces' classes and functions under
//    one name (ANGLE's prefix, libANGLE/Debug.h; its translator's
//    Traverser classes, defined many times; check_cpp.sh's two files).
pub const CODEGEN_EPOCH: u64 = 19
